WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:02.878
- I say it almost every day, like.

00:00:02.878 --> 00:00:05.550
When I finally go back home, back east,

00:00:05.550 --> 00:00:06.383
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:00:06.383 --> 00:00:07.910
- People are gonna think I'm lying,

00:00:07.910 --> 00:00:09.400
making up stories.
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:10.717
- About some of the
things that happen here.

00:00:10.717 --> 00:00:12.000
- [Mark] Where's back east for you?

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:13.340
- Washington, D.C.
- [Mark] D.C.?

00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:14.621
- That's why they call me DC.

00:00:14.621 --> 00:00:15.454
- [Mark] Oh, I see.

00:00:15.454 --> 00:00:17.430
- Yeah. My kids actually live in Virginia,

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:18.453
but-

00:00:18.453 --> 00:00:19.286
- [Mark] Yeah, it's crazy here.

00:00:19.286 --> 00:00:21.360
- It never ceases to, like,

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:22.612
I've been here seven years,

00:00:22.612 --> 00:00:27.150
and there's still shit that
can happen on a daily basis

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:29.660
that you just couldn't
make, you couldn't make up.

00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:30.629
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:00:30.629 --> 00:00:33.440
(sighs) DC, so you're
living on the street?

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:35.490
- Yeah, two blocks over, actually.

00:00:35.490 --> 00:00:37.340
- [Mark] How long have
you been on the street?

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:38.173
You got a tent?

00:00:38.173 --> 00:00:39.851
- Yeah, I got three of them, actually.

00:00:39.851 --> 00:00:40.684
- [Mark] Three of them?

00:00:40.684 --> 00:00:42.800
- Yeah, actually, today is
our street cleaning day.

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:43.670
- [Mark] Oh, so you're packing it up?

00:00:43.670 --> 00:00:45.970
- Yeah, every two weeks
we gotta do that shit.

00:00:46.964 --> 00:00:49.000
- [Mark] And then...

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:51.450
So what are you doing to make money?

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:52.900
- I sell pallets.

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:54.350
- [Mark] You sell pallets?
- Yeah.

00:00:54.350 --> 00:00:56.367
- [Mark] You're resourceful,
that's something different.

00:00:56.367 --> 00:00:58.557
- Yeah, and see, 'cause there's, uh,

00:00:59.573 --> 00:01:02.480
there's endless supply of them.

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:06.440
You know, you just have
to think of where to go

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:07.870
and when to go there.

00:01:07.870 --> 00:01:09.710
And after a while, certain
people will remember you,

00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:10.770
certain people will like you,

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:12.494
certain people will don't like you.

00:01:12.494 --> 00:01:15.100
You just have to find a way around things,

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:16.619
- [Mark] Yeah.
- to get the pallets.

00:01:16.619 --> 00:01:18.222
(DC and Mark laughing)

00:01:18.222 --> 00:01:19.342
- [Mark] And then, who
do you sell them to?

00:01:19.342 --> 00:01:20.920
- The pallet yards.

00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:23.070
There's one, the main
one's here on Series,

00:01:24.130 --> 00:01:25.797
right up the street from where I live.

00:01:25.797 --> 00:01:27.140
- [Mark] And you gotta
carry the pallet over down?

00:01:27.140 --> 00:01:28.433
- Yeah, on a basket,
I push it on a basket,

00:01:29.350 --> 00:01:30.527
or a pallet jack or something like that.

00:01:30.527 --> 00:01:31.400
- [Mark] Keeps you in good shape.

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:32.610
- Yeah, it does, actually.

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:37.045
Yeah, 'cause you'd be surprised, how...

00:01:37.045 --> 00:01:37.878
How...

00:01:40.314 --> 00:01:41.743
It's cardio-vascular.

00:01:41.743 --> 00:01:43.320
(DC chuckling)
- [Mark] Yeah,

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:47.000
you're in good shape
because of that currently.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:50.650
- Yeah, whenever I take
a break or some time off

00:01:50.650 --> 00:01:51.730
and then I try and do it again,

00:01:51.730 --> 00:01:54.412
I get surprised at how
winded I get, tired.

00:01:54.412 --> 00:01:56.350
(Mark laughing)
(DC chuckles)

00:01:56.350 --> 00:01:57.690
How many breaks I have to take.

00:01:57.690 --> 00:01:59.890
Damn, I do shit every day.

00:01:59.890 --> 00:02:01.040
Well, yeah, you're right.

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:03.500
- [Mark] So are you using currently?

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:05.173
- Yeah.
- [Mark] What are you using?

00:02:05.173 --> 00:02:06.439
- Um...

00:02:06.439 --> 00:02:07.433
(tongue clicking)

00:02:07.433 --> 00:02:08.960
Well, I smoke weed every day,

00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:11.160
I smoked weed every day
for most of my life.

00:02:12.290 --> 00:02:13.138
Cocaine.

00:02:13.138 --> 00:02:15.780
(police siren blaring)

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:17.440
Every once in a while, crystal meth,

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:18.790
but I don't really like it.

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:21.828
Sometimes PCP.

00:02:21.828 --> 00:02:24.363
- [Mark] What's, what's the difference?

00:02:24.363 --> 00:02:26.140
Did you try heroin too?

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:27.073
- No.

00:02:27.073 --> 00:02:28.280
- [Mark] You haven't tried?
- I refuse, I can't...

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:29.113
- [Mark] So what's-

00:02:29.113 --> 00:02:31.700
- It's too much dependency on that one.

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:33.323
You have to have it.

00:02:33.323 --> 00:02:35.040
- [Mark] But what's the difference?

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:35.873
- Okay.

00:02:35.873 --> 00:02:37.730
- [Mark] If someone's gonna take, uh...

00:02:37.730 --> 00:02:39.240
Is it crack you're doing?

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:40.525
- Yeah, and powder.

00:02:40.525 --> 00:02:42.450
- [Mark] And powder?
- Yeah.

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:43.283
'Cause there's a...

00:02:45.210 --> 00:02:46.713
The difference between crack and powder,

00:02:46.713 --> 00:02:49.700
it's just the... the urgency of the rush,

00:02:49.700 --> 00:02:51.343
which is, it's the same rush.

00:02:52.490 --> 00:02:53.560
It's the urgency of the rush.

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:55.850
- [Mark] With the crack it's faster?

00:02:55.850 --> 00:02:57.130
- Much more,

00:02:57.130 --> 00:02:58.800
much, much more potent

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:00.530
and leaves much, much more, faster.

00:03:00.530 --> 00:03:01.780
'cause it's much,

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:02.920
it's uh...

00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:04.200
More urgency.

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:05.632
So then...

00:03:05.632 --> 00:03:07.460
And then, okay.

00:03:07.460 --> 00:03:09.160
And then it's just like, over. (laughing)

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:13.320
So then, it creates another
urgency to keep me going.

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:14.893
- [ Mark] You need more?
- Yeah.

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:18.444
- [Mark] And PCP, tell me about that?

00:03:18.444 --> 00:03:19.895
- Oh man.

00:03:19.895 --> 00:03:22.250
So, I used to smoke that a
lot when I was younger too,

00:03:22.250 --> 00:03:24.560
but in D.C, we call it "Love Boat",

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:25.860
or "angel dust" basically.

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:30.120
Over here, it's funny 'cause,

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:33.000
like, this is where they
were getting it, in LA,

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:34.923
it's like LA, DC pipeline, yeah.

00:03:35.942 --> 00:03:36.775
So...

00:03:37.810 --> 00:03:39.530
I stopped for a long time.

00:03:39.530 --> 00:03:40.512
I really-

00:03:40.512 --> 00:03:45.148
- [Mark] What does that do for
you, as opposed to cocaine?

00:03:45.148 --> 00:03:47.287
- It kills your motor skills.

00:03:47.287 --> 00:03:48.890
(Mark laughs)
(DC chuckles)

00:03:48.890 --> 00:03:50.209
- [Mark] What's the upside?

00:03:50.209 --> 00:03:51.605
- I don't really see one,

00:03:51.605 --> 00:03:53.249
I don't remember why I
was smoking. (chuckling)

00:03:53.249 --> 00:03:54.840
- [Mark] And crystal
meth? Tell me about that.

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:55.931
- Nothing.

00:03:55.931 --> 00:03:56.930
Just nothing.

00:03:56.930 --> 00:03:58.070
It's like Tylenol.

00:03:58.070 --> 00:03:59.730
Yeah, it's false (indistinct)

00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:00.857
You're tired and you don't know it,

00:04:00.857 --> 00:04:03.325
you're a zombie.
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:04:03.325 --> 00:04:04.990
- At least with cocaine, I...

00:04:04.990 --> 00:04:06.233
okay, if you go,

00:04:07.650 --> 00:04:09.060
say, another 30 minutes or an hour

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:11.853
without any, and your body catches up,

00:04:13.824 --> 00:04:15.120
you're just shutting down entirely,

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:16.703
Crystal meth is more really...

00:04:17.714 --> 00:04:18.877
you have to be, like,
knocked out or some shit.

00:04:18.877 --> 00:04:22.160
- [Mark] What's the most
popular drug on the street here?

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:22.993
Heroin?

00:04:22.993 --> 00:04:24.970
- No, crack.
- [Mark] Crack?

00:04:24.970 --> 00:04:26.670
- But crystal meth is catching up,

00:04:27.980 --> 00:04:29.430
rapidly. (chuckling)

00:04:29.430 --> 00:04:32.240
because some people consider it

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:34.270
like a graduation

00:04:34.270 --> 00:04:36.620
because they don't have
to spend as much money.

00:04:38.910 --> 00:04:40.840
But it's, it's a false...

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:42.360
See,

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:43.740
I, uh...

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:44.940
I compare it to Tylenol.

00:04:45.890 --> 00:04:49.170
Tylenol doesn't really
kill pain or stop pain,

00:04:49.170 --> 00:04:51.418
it tricks your brain into
saying there's no pain.

00:04:51.418 --> 00:04:53.247
For some people that does work,

00:04:53.247 --> 00:04:54.460
I think crystal meth is the same way.

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:55.770
It's tricks your brain,

00:04:55.770 --> 00:04:59.840
thinking you're getting a
rush, but you're really not.

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:01.640
- [Mark] Tell me about your childhood

00:05:01.640 --> 00:05:02.957
I'm sure you've talked about it before.

00:05:02.957 --> 00:05:05.986
- No, not really, I didn't
open up at all about that.

00:05:05.986 --> 00:05:07.400
I don't really do.

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:08.603
I grew up in Chicago.

00:05:11.081 --> 00:05:11.914
Uh...

00:05:12.940 --> 00:05:13.790
- [Mark] That's where I'm from too,

00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:15.460
but in I think I was in
a different neighborhood.

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:16.370
- Probably so.
(Mark laughs)

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:18.143
Where you born in Cook
County Hospital too?

00:05:18.143 --> 00:05:19.237
- [Mark] Yeah, I wasn't, no.

00:05:19.237 --> 00:05:21.555
- You might've been from like
Naperville, or some shit.

00:05:21.555 --> 00:05:22.388
- [Mark] Yeah, exactly (chuckling)

00:05:22.388 --> 00:05:23.484
Evanston or Skokie.

00:05:23.484 --> 00:05:24.450
(Mark chuckling)

00:05:24.450 --> 00:05:27.250
Yeah, and I grew up in Chicago
'till I was 10 years old.

00:05:28.670 --> 00:05:29.620
My mom...

00:05:33.050 --> 00:05:34.127
She had me,

00:05:34.127 --> 00:05:37.777
11 months after, she had my
sister, we had different dads.

00:05:37.777 --> 00:05:41.533
She was in college, but she had like...

00:05:41.533 --> 00:05:45.033
she had tendencies to
run the streets and do,

00:05:47.070 --> 00:05:47.990
do wild stuff.

00:05:47.990 --> 00:05:50.200
I remember she used to take us to,

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:52.584
bars and racetracks.

00:05:52.584 --> 00:05:54.294
- [Mark] At what age?

00:05:54.294 --> 00:05:56.799
- [DC] Four, five...
three, four, five, yeah.

00:05:56.799 --> 00:05:57.632
Yeah, and

00:05:58.682 --> 00:05:59.515
uh...

00:05:59.515 --> 00:06:00.348
Pool halls, racetracks.

00:06:00.348 --> 00:06:01.181
Shit like that.

00:06:02.774 --> 00:06:04.490
- [Mark] How old was
your mom? At that time.

00:06:04.490 --> 00:06:06.147
- [DC] At the time?

00:06:06.147 --> 00:06:07.249
- [Mark] She was in her twenties.

00:06:07.249 --> 00:06:08.180
- [DC] Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah,

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:09.230
mid twenties, prolly.

00:06:10.590 --> 00:06:12.187
She got in trouble, and...

00:06:13.940 --> 00:06:15.960
We gotta go to foster care,

00:06:15.960 --> 00:06:17.720
me and my sister and my little brother.

00:06:17.720 --> 00:06:18.801
- [Mark] You said your mom got in trouble,

00:06:18.801 --> 00:06:19.634
did she got put in prison?

00:06:19.634 --> 00:06:20.710
- [DC] Yeah.

00:06:20.710 --> 00:06:22.450
- [Mark] For what?

00:06:22.450 --> 00:06:25.100
- [DC] She still won't let
me know completely, but...

00:06:26.190 --> 00:06:28.240
Somebody died. (chuckling)

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:29.120
Yeah,

00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:29.953
but, uh...

00:06:31.240 --> 00:06:34.770
She ended up being able to get us back.

00:06:34.770 --> 00:06:36.731
She got out, she got us back,

00:06:36.731 --> 00:06:39.310
and she was a Born again
Christian after that.

00:06:39.310 --> 00:06:40.143
Yeah.

00:06:41.250 --> 00:06:45.080
But I still remember her,
and, you know, who she is.

00:06:45.080 --> 00:06:46.830
Born again Christian stuff, anyway.

00:06:48.005 --> 00:06:48.838
(DC sighting)

00:06:48.838 --> 00:06:50.290
She got a job transfer,

00:06:50.290 --> 00:06:51.823
when I was 10 years old,

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:55.920
to, uh, Washington DC.

00:06:55.920 --> 00:06:58.410
She thought it was better,

00:06:58.410 --> 00:07:00.930
'cause she's in the building-

00:07:00.930 --> 00:07:02.190
The project building I lived in

00:07:02.190 --> 00:07:04.820
was a Gangster Disciple control building.

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:06.080
And they started, uh, you know,

00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:07.690
they recruit,

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:10.540
like, like boys at a certain age.

00:07:10.540 --> 00:07:11.910
And when they see cert-

00:07:11.910 --> 00:07:13.740
they saw certain things in
me that they wanted to use.

00:07:13.740 --> 00:07:15.020
- [Mark] So the Disciples wanted you?

00:07:15.020 --> 00:07:15.902
- [DC] Yeah.

00:07:15.902 --> 00:07:17.660
And they wanted to do with
teaching me, and shit.

00:07:17.660 --> 00:07:18.493
Good shit.

00:07:18.493 --> 00:07:20.450
And she saw it,

00:07:20.450 --> 00:07:21.483
she didn't like it.

00:07:23.716 --> 00:07:24.883
She figured...

00:07:26.770 --> 00:07:28.460
I had to get away.

00:07:28.460 --> 00:07:30.733
Ironically, we went to D.C.

00:07:30.733 --> 00:07:32.150
D.C. was no better.

00:07:32.150 --> 00:07:33.110
That's when I...

00:07:34.116 --> 00:07:36.410
was really, really, really cracked out.

00:07:36.410 --> 00:07:37.670
- [Mark] The Disciples
were in Chicago or D.C.?

00:07:37.670 --> 00:07:39.210
- Yeah, that was in Chicago.

00:07:39.210 --> 00:07:40.950
We moved to DC to get away from that.

00:07:40.950 --> 00:07:42.940
- [Mark] I see.
- Yeah.

00:07:42.940 --> 00:07:43.953
DC was no better.

00:07:45.690 --> 00:07:47.251
We didn't know it.

00:07:47.251 --> 00:07:48.620
- [Mark] Was there gangs
there? What's wrong?

00:07:48.620 --> 00:07:50.860
- No, it's just, just utter poverty.

00:07:50.860 --> 00:07:52.390
No so much gangs, it's just...

00:07:52.390 --> 00:07:53.453
poverty and poverty.

00:07:54.800 --> 00:07:56.780
Especially then, between-

00:07:56.780 --> 00:07:58.420
Marion Barry, 'member Marion.

00:07:58.420 --> 00:07:59.253
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:07:59.253 --> 00:08:00.086
- That was the same year, 1991.

00:08:01.142 --> 00:08:03.660
Yeah...

00:08:05.090 --> 00:08:07.793
She wanted us to go to better schools.

00:08:09.210 --> 00:08:11.203
After like maybe, like, two years,

00:08:12.440 --> 00:08:14.963
she had- we moved to Virginia,

00:08:16.340 --> 00:08:18.740
Northern Virginia suburbs of D.C.

00:08:18.740 --> 00:08:21.217
started a better life, better schools.

00:08:21.217 --> 00:08:23.050
And it's where the irony comes in.

00:08:23.050 --> 00:08:25.203
That's where I got in all the trouble.

00:08:26.390 --> 00:08:27.758
- [Mark] Trouble?

00:08:27.758 --> 00:08:28.591
- Yeah.

00:08:28.591 --> 00:08:29.424
- [Mark] What kind of trouble?

00:08:30.510 --> 00:08:31.423
- When I was 13,

00:08:33.940 --> 00:08:35.420
I got my first...

00:08:36.480 --> 00:08:38.270
When I was 13, was the
first time I smoked weed,

00:08:38.270 --> 00:08:41.120
first time I drank, first time I had sex.

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:43.083
First time I bust a gun,

00:08:44.520 --> 00:08:46.370
first time I drove a car,

00:08:46.370 --> 00:08:48.370
the first, my first felony,

00:08:48.370 --> 00:08:50.160
my first charge, period.

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:51.560
First gun charge.

00:08:51.560 --> 00:08:54.940
All that shit happened when I was 13.

00:08:54.940 --> 00:08:58.540
Yeah, and so, I was a convicted felon,

00:08:58.540 --> 00:09:01.020
actually, before I ever had sex.

00:09:01.020 --> 00:09:02.520
- [Mark] How much prison time you did?

00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:03.440
- In my life?

00:09:03.440 --> 00:09:04.273
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:09:04.273 --> 00:09:05.683
- I mean, I dunno.

00:09:05.683 --> 00:09:06.516
(Mark and DC chuckling)

00:09:06.516 --> 00:09:07.349
- [Mark] How many-

00:09:07.349 --> 00:09:08.182
(DC chuckling)

00:09:08.182 --> 00:09:10.267
- [Mark] What have you been in prison for?

00:09:10.267 --> 00:09:11.804
- Oh, that (chuckling)

00:09:11.804 --> 00:09:13.070
Prison or jail?

00:09:13.070 --> 00:09:14.070
- [Mark] Either one.

00:09:16.370 --> 00:09:18.780
- Mostly just not doing what they say.

00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:21.850
I never really done anything,

00:09:22.920 --> 00:09:24.380
like,

00:09:24.380 --> 00:09:27.330
so heinous that you
have to be locked away.

00:09:27.330 --> 00:09:28.410
It's mostly...

00:09:28.410 --> 00:09:31.010
Okay, you know, probation and these rules

00:09:31.010 --> 00:09:32.010
- [Mark] You just gotta follow the rules.

00:09:32.010 --> 00:09:33.117
- I don't follow any rules.

00:09:33.117 --> 00:09:35.097
"We'll give you one more chance."

00:09:35.097 --> 00:09:38.314
"You're disrespecting the
judge." All that stuff.

00:09:38.314 --> 00:09:40.220
(chuckling)

00:09:40.220 --> 00:09:43.535
I gotta problem with authority, I guess.

00:09:43.535 --> 00:09:45.180
- [Mark] How old are you now?

00:09:45.180 --> 00:09:48.000
- I'll be 38 in two months.

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:49.953
- [Mark] Where exactly do you
see yourself in five years?

00:09:51.352 --> 00:09:52.352
- Back with my kids,

00:09:53.290 --> 00:09:55.100
with a story to tell,

00:09:55.100 --> 00:09:57.135
to help somebody else not do this.

00:09:57.135 --> 00:09:59.060
(chuckling)

00:09:59.060 --> 00:10:00.060
That's, that's where

00:10:01.303 --> 00:10:02.414
I'd like to be in five years.

00:10:02.414 --> 00:10:04.475
That's where I will be in five years.

00:10:04.475 --> 00:10:06.850
I'll be back with my kids.

00:10:06.850 --> 00:10:08.320
And an inspiration to people,

00:10:08.320 --> 00:10:11.311
'cause if he can overcome this,

00:10:11.311 --> 00:10:12.985
you can overcome anything.

00:10:12.985 --> 00:10:14.640
And I know I will overcome this.

00:10:14.640 --> 00:10:15.544
- [Mark] This is the bottom, man.

00:10:15.544 --> 00:10:16.377
- Yeah!

00:10:16.377 --> 00:10:17.210
- [Mark] This is the bottom.

00:10:17.210 --> 00:10:19.160
- Yes, this is the hardest way of life.

00:10:21.630 --> 00:10:25.430
It's funny, because you think in America

00:10:27.511 --> 00:10:29.800
no one would have to live like this.

00:10:29.800 --> 00:10:31.523
And most of America has no clue.

00:10:33.150 --> 00:10:35.244
And it's really (indistinct)

00:10:35.244 --> 00:10:37.150
Only thing is, noticing it, seeing it

00:10:37.150 --> 00:10:39.093
doesn't really help you to not do it.

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:43.253
It's very pacified, living on the street,

00:10:44.600 --> 00:10:46.930
where you don't have to pay rent,

00:10:46.930 --> 00:10:49.199
you don't have to pay any bills.

00:10:49.199 --> 00:10:50.749
I mean, the weather permits it.

00:10:51.900 --> 00:10:53.530
They bring you food,

00:10:53.530 --> 00:10:54.430
bring you clothes.

00:10:56.700 --> 00:10:58.250
What else? I mean, what...

00:10:58.250 --> 00:11:00.168
Any money you can get,

00:11:00.168 --> 00:11:01.418
goes right away on drugs.

00:11:02.860 --> 00:11:03.990
It's all right, because

00:11:03.990 --> 00:11:06.687
we'll feed you, we'll clothed you.

00:11:06.687 --> 00:11:08.320
You can live here for free.

00:11:08.320 --> 00:11:09.153
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:11:10.730 --> 00:11:11.930
- [DC] There's nowhere else like this

00:11:11.930 --> 00:11:13.257
anywhere, anywhere.

00:11:14.750 --> 00:11:16.343
You can't live on a sidewalk.

00:11:18.129 --> 00:11:19.880
(Mark and DC chuckling)

00:11:19.880 --> 00:11:22.140
Even if it's summertime,

00:11:22.140 --> 00:11:22.973
you gotta hurry up and say

00:11:22.973 --> 00:11:24.410
get your ass off the sidewalk.

